# Package Manager — Always Use pnpm

## Rule

This project uses **pnpm exclusively**. Never run `npm install` or `yarn` in this project.

## Installing dependencies

Always use pnpm when adding or installing packages:

```bash
# Correct
pnpm add tesseract.js pdfjs-dist
pnpm install

# NEVER do this — it only updates package-lock.json, not pnpm-lock.yaml
npm install tesseract.js pdfjs-dist   # WRONG
```

## Why this matters

Vercel CI runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. If `pnpm-lock.yaml` is out of sync with `package.json`, the build fails immediately. Using `npm install` silently updates `package-lock.json` but never touches `pnpm-lock.yaml`, causing this exact failure.

## If pnpm is not available in the terminal

Run this once to enable it:

```bash
npm install -g corepack@latest
corepack enable
# pnpm is now available
pnpm add <package>
```

## Recovery (if npm install was accidentally used)

If `npm install` was already run and `pnpm-lock.yaml` is stale, recover with:

```bash
pnpm import          # regenerates pnpm-lock.yaml from package-lock.json
git add pnpm-lock.yaml
git commit -m "fix: sync pnpm-lock.yaml"
```

## Verification before committing

After adding any package, confirm both lockfiles are consistent:

```bash
Select-String "new-package-name" pnpm-lock.yaml   # must appear
```
